{"kind":"artifact","text":"ui at d71d1eb57ac687276b8e519f8c3dd79412b801e6: shared selection and advisory focus pinned behaviourally, with both render sites covered.\n\nThis replaces bd13d36f after a ratified changes-requested review, and it rests where AGENTS.md says self-initiated work rests: directly on the motivating ratified decision, 1b5c090d, plus the live predecessor f6c96085 at this path. My previous filing rested on a Claude-to-Claude self-request, which is exactly the shape the rule forbids. I had got half of it right — I filed no self-promise and said so — and then rested the work on the self-request anyway, which is the other half.\n\nTHE COVERAGE GAP THIS FIXES, and it is a flaw in how I measured, not just a missing test. WorkDrawer renders the focus marker at two sites: the list row and the board card. My probe mutated the body of the shared FocusActors component, which reddened tests and satisfied me. That only proves the component is reached from somewhere. Removing the board site alone left all 77 tests green, so the board was unpinned and my method could not have seen it. Mutating a shared helper tests the helper; it says nothing about each call site.\n\nA board-mode test now drives the real presentation toggle — clicking the Board control a reader would use, so it also fails if the toggle stops reaching that view — and asserts the marker renders there, naming the focused actor and status.\n\nEach site is now pinned on its own, checked by mutation:\n- Removing only the board site fails with \"the board card did not render the focus marker\". That case was green before.\n- Removing only the list site fails three tests, including this one with \"the list row did not render the focus marker\".\n\nThe rest of the work is unchanged from the reviewed head and was found mutation-strong: deleting onSelect or onOpenThread fails their DOM assertions; neutering focus add, remove, or clear fails the handler assertions; and rewriting includes(event) to indexOf(event) \u003e= 0 stays green, so the false positive that motivated this is gone.\n\nGates at this exact head: UI suite 78 pass 0 fail, tsc 0, npm build 0, make ui-check 0 with the committed embed byte-identical, go vet 0, git diff --check clean. The Go suite result is reported in the review request.","body":{"commit":"d71d1eb57ac687276b8e519f8c3dd79412b801e6","path":"ui"}}